rota lap 5363, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; take in the concrete fact at the door before any argument, so the lap RAN the two readings and crossed them rather than reasoning about whether form ought to predict outcome
think Round open found a stale roster pass holding the lock from launch_head 94df5c9c2b, four commits back, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved. Verified its cwd through /proc before signaling -- this tree, my own ship -- then TERMed the named pid, which is the tool's own instruction and never a pattern-resolved kill.
think The earth reading was rank_outcome_scan falsifier_faulted=10 of 12 on this lane's elder ranked page: 6 structurally incapable, 3 already settled, 1 misaimed. That is five sixths of my own lane's stated falsifiers unable to do their job, and it is a fact rather than an argument.
think Beside it sat falsifier_reach_scan, landed by this seat four hours earlier, whose closing handoff reads 27 runnable falsifiers is the number to grow. That sentence is a projection about OUTCOME made from a reading of FORM, and it named no falsifier of its own. Nothing crossed the two instruments, so the lap crossed them.
think Checked absence of the SUBJECT rather than of my names, which is the trap the card's bakery account booked: git grep for every reader of falsifier_incapable, page_narrative_only and falsifier_reach found the two scans, their witnesses, two papers and the card, and no crossing.
think Reused rather than rewrote: the class comes from falsifier_reach_scan --list, whose region lines already carry a class and a start line, and the fault from rank_outcome_scan --explain. A second class test written here would be a second rule to drift, which is what two peer lanes spent this morning sweeping out of glow.
think Ranked pages are DISCOVERED by carrying a ## The ranking heading rather than listed, so a third joins on the lap it lands; rows are its ### N. sections, ended at the next such heading or the next top-level one.
obs The crossing reads pages_found=2, rows_read=21, form_runnable=0. Not one speculative row on either ranked page states a falsifier naming a path, so the informative cell is EMPTY and the scan reads verdict=underdetermined rather than a correlation it cannot support. That is the rank scan's own incapable verdict arriving in the measurement rather than in a page.
obs The reason is structural rather than careless, and it is worth more than the number: a proposal's falsifier is written before its instrument exists, so it has no path to name. The elder page's three runnable regions are all ERRATA, each citing the scan that graded its row. The handoff was aimed at the wrong moment in a page's life, and is re-aimed by erratum to an erratum owes a runnable falsifier.
obs The rates where rows do stand are 0.7500 over four and 0.7778 over nine, resting on three faults and seven. Printed and named as a reading with no power rather than a null result with power behind it, since a rate nobody prints cannot be told from a rate nobody took. Silence sits in the denominator and never the numerator, so both are lower bounds.
obs The stronger reading needs no statistics: not one of the ten faults is a fault a form test can see. Row 4 named a real scan and fired at radius zero; row 9's proposed witness prints parking properties while its falsifier is about backlog; row 2 fires on seated code rather than the future process. Form asks whether somebody can act; outcome asks whether acting discriminates.
obs MINE -- my first verdict turned on a runnable row EXISTING rather than being GRADED, so an unread proposal would have unlocked a crossing with nothing in its cell. The pen caught it and now proves both sides of exactly that distinction: runnable_row_present and runnable_cell_still_empty in one pen, crossed_once_runnable_graded in the next.
obs Widened the scan mid-build after finding it conflated a silent erratum with an unread row, since rank_outcome emits an explain line only for a fault it can name. Reading the elder's own **Row N erratum:** lines tells the two apart; rows_graded moved 11 to 13 and agreed with the rank scan's own falsifier_read=12 on that page.
obs The wall it can honestly hold is narrow and decidable: a ranked row carrying no falsifier region at all, gated at zero, since no later erratum can ever grade it. The crossing itself gates nothing.
